{"schema_version":"1.9.2","id":"JLSEC-2026-1444","published":"2026-11-23T20:01:46.351Z","modified":"2026-11-23T20:15:05.539201506Z","upstream":["CVE-2026-70461","EUVD-2026-58043"],"details":"rsync 3.2.5 before 3.5.0 contains a heap out-of-bounds write vulnerability that allows remote unauthenticated attackers to write one attacker-controlled byte past the end of a heap allocation by supplying a crafted files-from entry. Attackers can trigger the vulnerability against a read-only rsync daemon module by providing a files-from entry containing both an interior and trailing backslash, causing the `add_implied_include()` function to under-count the trailing backslash when sizing the destination buffer.","affected":[{"package":{"name":"rsync_jll","ecosystem":"Julia","purl":"pkg:julia/rsync_jll?uuid=191d6b87-264a-55f5-a0e2-c8fbce9a1ce0"},"ranges":[{"type":"SEMVER","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"3.5.0+0"}]}],"database_specific":{"source":"https://github.com/JuliaLang/SecurityAdvisories.jl/tree/generated/osv/2026/JLSEC-2026-1444.json"}}],"references":[{"type":"WEB","url":"https://github.com/RsyncProject/rsync/releases/tag/v3.5.0"},{"type":"WEB","url":"https://github.com/RsyncProject/rsync/security/advisories/GHSA-jhxm-j4mq-3fj4"},{"type":"WEB","url":"https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/rsync-heap-out-of-bounds-write-via-files-from-entry"}],"database_specific":{"license":"CC-BY-4.0","sources":[{"affected":{"samba:rsync":[">= 3.2.5, < 3.5.0"]},"database_specific":{"status":"Analyzed"},"html_url":"https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-70461","id":"CVE-2026-70461","imported":"2026-11-21T02:56:05.001Z","modified":"2026-10-24T16:10:00.153Z","published":"2026-08-13T15:20:00.117Z","url":"https://services.nvd.nist.gov/rest/json/cves/2.0?cveId=CVE-2026-70461"},{"html_url":"https://euvd.enisa.europa.eu/vulnerability/EUVD-2026-58043","id":"EUVD-2026-58043","imported":"2026-11-21T02:56:06.499Z","modified":"2026-08-14T16:51:24Z","published":"2026-08-13T14:42:49Z","url":"https